<%- await include('_nav') %>

<%# WHICH BUILDING'S LINEN.
    Each of Igatpuri's four buildings keeps its own store, so the shelf, the
    day's issues, the wash and the write-offs are all facts about a building.
    Forty-three of the forty-five running rooms are one building; for those
    `blocks` is empty and none of this appears. %>
<% if (blocks && blocks.length) { %>
  <div class="card blockbar">
    <div class="bb-row">
      <span class="bb-lab">Building</span>
        <% blocks.forEach(function(b){ %>
          <a class="btn <%= blockId === b.id ? '' : 'ghost' %> small"
             href="<%= url('/facility/laundry') %>?rr=<%= rr.id %>&block=<%= b.id %>"><%= b.name %>
             <span class="muted" style="font-weight:400">· <%= b.total_beds %> beds</span></a>
        <% }); %>
      <% if (orphans) { %>
        <a class="btn <%= viewNone ? '' : 'ghost' %> small"
           href="<%= url('/facility/laundry') %>?rr=<%= rr.id %>&block=none">No building
           <span class="pill" style="margin-left:5px"><%= orphans %></span></a>
      <% } %>
    </div>
  </div>
<% } %>
<% if (viewNone && orphans) { %>
  <div class="note warn" style="margin-bottom:14px">
    <b>Records made before <%= rr.name %> had buildings.</b>
    These <%= orphans %> row<%= orphans === 1 ? '' : 's' %> belong to no building, because none
    existed when they were written. They are shown here so they are not lost — nothing new can be
    recorded against "no building", because a round is done in one building and linen sits on one
    shelf. Read them, close out anything still open, and the list will empty itself.
  </div>
<% } else if (viewNone) { %>
  <%# The button that leads here only appears when there is something to see,
      so arriving with nothing means the list has been worked through — or the
      address was typed. Either way, saying "0 rows belong to no building" as
      though it were a finding would be the screen inventing a problem. %>
  <div class="note" style="margin-bottom:14px">
    Nothing at <%= rr.name %> is on record without a building.
  </div>
<% } %>

<% if (needBlock) { %>
  <%# NOT AN ERROR — A QUESTION THE REGISTER CANNOT ANSWER FOR HIM.
      Defaulting to the first building would work out one building's ledger
      from another's opening figure, and the arithmetic would look perfectly
      sound while being about the wrong shelf. %>
  <div class="note warn">
    <b>Choose the building above.</b>
    <%= rr.name %> stands in <%= blocks.length %> buildings and each keeps its own linen —
    nothing is defaulted, because a ledger opened from the wrong shelf is wrong in a way
    that looks right.
  </div>
<% } else { %>

<%
  /* Names come from the seeded schedule, not from a map kept by hand here — a
     view that carries its own copy of the contract's item list is a second
     place for it to be wrong. */
  const ITEMS = Object.fromEntries(schedule.map(x => [x.item_type, x.name]));
  const d10 = v => String(v).slice(0, 10);
%>

<%# THE ORDER OF THIS PAGE IS THE ORDER OF THE WORK.
    Send, receive, read the return, read the dispatch register. It used to open
    on five summary tiles and keep both forms below them, which put the two
    things a supervisor comes here to DO underneath the things an officer comes
    here to READ. The tiles have not been removed; they have been put where a
    summary belongs, at the head of the registers it summarises. %>

<% if (unapproved.length || noVendor.length) { %>
  <div class="note err" style="margin-bottom:14px">
    <b><%= unapproved.length + noVendor.length %> of the last <%= rows.length %> dispatches</b> went to a
    washing centre the Railway has not approved<% if (unapprovedPieces) { %> —
    <%= fmtInt(unapprovedPieces) %> pieces<% } %>.
    <% if (noVendor.length) { %>
      <%= noVendor.length %> of them name no washing centre at all, which is the same breach wearing a
      different hat: the linen went somewhere and the register cannot say where.
    <% } %>
    <div style="margin-top:6px;font-size:12px">
      Clause C1 makes this a deficiency in its own right, quite apart from how well the linen came back.
      Raise it from the <a href="<%= url('/inspections/new') %>?rr=<%= rr.id %>">inspection checklist</a> so
      it carries into the month; no amount is computed here.
    </div>
  </div>
<% } %>

<% if (!vendor) { %>
  <div class="note warn" style="margin-bottom:14px">
    No approved laundry is on record for <b><%= rr.name %></b>. Clause C1 treats washing at any other
    source as a deficiency, so the approved washing centre should be recorded before dispatches are entered.
  </div>
<% } else if (!vendor.is_approved) { %>
  <div class="note err" style="margin-bottom:14px">
    <b><%= vendor.name %></b> is attached to this running room but is not marked approved.
  </div>
<% } %>

<%# ------------------------------------------------------------ 1. SEND %>
<div class="card" style="margin-bottom:14px">
  <div class="card-h"><h3>Send to the wash</h3>
    <span class="sub"><% if (vendor) { %><%= vendor.name %><% if (vendor.licence_no) { %> · licence <%= vendor.licence_no %><% } %>
      <% } else { %>no approved washing centre on record<% } %></span></div>
  <div class="card-b">
    <%# WHAT HAS ALREADY GONE TODAY, BEFORE HE TYPES.
        The daily linen register prints a "Sent to wash" column, so a man
        filling that screen can see he has already sent. This page held the
        same dispatches in a register of the last forty, by date, with no
        total — which is not the same as being able to see them. Found by the
        officer thinking about the man rather than the code: send twenty bed
        sheets from the daily screen in the morning, come here in the
        afternoon, forget, and send the same twenty again.

        It is stated, not enforced. A second consignment of the same item on
        the same day is ordinary — the laundry man comes twice — so refusing
        it would make the register lie about a real dispatch. %>
    <% if (sentTodayTotal) { %>
      <div class="note" style="margin-bottom:12px">
        <b>Already gone today<% if (block) { %> from <%= block.name %><% } %>:</b>
        <%= Object.keys(sentToday).map(function(k){
              return sentToday[k].qty + ' × ' + (ITEMS[k] || k)
                + (sentToday[k].consignments > 1 ? ' (' + sentToday[k].consignments + ' consignments)' : '');
            }).join(' · ') %>
        <div class="muted" style="font-size:11.3px;margin-top:5px">
          Sending the same item again today is not refused — the laundry man may come twice —
          but check this is a second bundle and not the first one entered again. The daily
          linen register and this page write to the same record, so a consignment entered
          there is already counted here.
        </div>
      </div>
    <% } else { %>
      <div class="muted" style="font-size:11.5px;margin-bottom:12px">
        Nothing has gone to the wash today<% if (block) { %> from <%= block.name %><% } %>.
      </div>
    <% } %>
    <% if (can('stay.manage') && !viewNone) { %>
    <form method="post" action="<%= url('/facility/laundry') %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="rr" value="<%= rr.id %>">
        <% if (blockId) { %><input type="hidden" name="block" value="<%= blockId %>"><% } %>
      <div class="row" style="gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end">
        <div style="flex:0 0 150px"><label class="fl">Sent on</label>
          <input class="fi" type="date" name="dispatch_date" value="<%= date %>" max="<%= todayStr %>" required></div>
        <div style="flex:0 0 190px"><label class="fl">Item</label>
          <select class="fi" name="item_type" id="washitem"
                  data-sent='<%- JSON.stringify(Object.keys(sentToday).reduce(function(a,k){ a[k]=sentToday[k].qty; return a; }, {})) %>'>
            <% Object.keys(ITEMS).forEach(function(k){ %><option value="<%= k %>"><%= ITEMS[k] %></option><% }); %>
          </select>
          <%# The line under the box names the item he is looking at, so the
              warning is about the thing in front of him rather than a list he
              has to read. %>
          <div class="muted" id="washitemsent" style="font-size:11px;margin-top:4px"></div></div>
        <div style="flex:0 0 120px"><label class="fl">Quantity sent</label>
          <input class="fi" type="number" min="1" name="quantity_sent" required></div>
        <%# WHERE IT IS COMING FROM.
            Almost every dispatch is used linen stripped off the beds, which was
            never on the fresh shelf — so the shelf figure is right to ignore
            it, and that is the default. Linen taken off the SHELF and sent was
            on it, and the shelf must drop by that much or the same pieces are
            counted twice: once on the shelf and once at the wash. Nobody was
            ever asked, so the register could not tell the two apart. %>
        <div style="flex:0 0 210px"><label class="fl">Taken from</label>
          <select class="fi" name="from_pool">
            <option value="used">Used linen off the beds</option>
            <option value="shelf">Fresh stock on the shelf</option>
          </select>
          <div class="muted" style="font-size:10.5px;margin-top:3px">
            Fresh stock sent to the wash comes off the shelf figure.
          </div></div>
        <div style="flex:1 1 200px"><label class="fl">Washing centre</label>
          <select class="fi" name="vendor_id">
            <option value="">— not recorded —</option>
            <% vendors.forEach(function(v){ %>
              <option value="<%= v.id %>" <%= vendor && v.id===vendor.id?'selected':'' %>><%= v.name %><%= v.is_approved ? '' : ' (not approved)' %></option>
            <% }); %>
          </select></div>
        <div style="flex:0 0 150px"><label class="fl">Invoice no.</label>
          <input class="fi" type="text" name="invoice_no" placeholder="as on the bill"></div>
        <div style="flex:1 1 180px"><label class="fl">Remarks</label>
          <input class="fi" type="text" name="quality_remarks" placeholder="challan, condition"></div>
        <div><button class="btn" type="submit">Save dispatch</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="muted" style="font-size:11.3px;margin-top:8px">
        Nothing is received here. When this linen comes back it is taken in below, against this
        consignment, so the shortfall between what went and what returned stays attached to the
        batch it belongs to. The invoice is what makes the washing centre provable — clause C1.
      </div>
          <script>
      (function () {
        var sel = document.getElementById('washitem');
        var out = document.getElementById('washitemsent');
        if (!sel || !out) return;
        var sent = {};
        try { sent = JSON.parse(sel.getAttribute('data-sent') || '{}'); } catch (e) { return; }
        function say() {
          var n = sent[sel.value] || 0;
          var name = sel.options[sel.selectedIndex].textContent.trim();
          out.textContent = n
            ? n + ' ' + name.toLowerCase() + (n === 1 ? '' : 's') + ' already went today — check this is a second bundle'
            : '';
          out.className = n ? 'st warn' : 'muted';
          out.style.fontSize = '11px';
          out.style.marginTop = '4px';
        }
        sel.addEventListener('change', say); say();
      })();
      </script>
</form>
    <% } else { %>
      <div class="muted" style="font-size:12.5px">Your role has view access only.</div>
    <% } %>
  </div>
</div>

<%# --------------------------------------------------------- 2. RECEIVE
    A consignment coming back is the second half of the only transaction this
    page has. It was once a small link in the fifth column of a table that
    scrolls sideways, which is the same as not being on the screen at all. %>
<% const openRows = rows.filter(function(r){ return r.quantity_returned < r.quantity_sent; }); %>
<% if (can('stay.manage') && !viewNone && openRows.length) { %>
<div class="card" style="margin-bottom:14px">
  <div class="card-h"><h3>Coming back from the wash</h3>
    <span class="sub"><%= openRows.length %> consignment<%= openRows.length === 1 ? '' : 's' %> still out</span></div>
  <div class="card-b">
    <div class="muted" style="font-size:11.5px;margin-bottom:10px">
      Each block below is one consignment, named by what went out and the day it went.
      Take the linen back against the block it belongs to — that is what keeps the
      shortfall visible.
    </div>
    <% openRows.forEach(function(r){ %>
      <form method="post" action="<%= url('/facility/laundry/' + r.id + '/return') %>"
            style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;padding:11px 12px;margin-bottom:10px">
        <div style="font-size:13px;margin-bottom:9px">
          <b><%= ITEMS[r.item_type] || r.item_type %></b>
          <span class="muted">— <%= r.quantity_sent %> sent on <%= d10(r.dispatch_date) %><%
            if (r.vendor_name) { %> to <%= r.vendor_name %><% } %><%
            if (r.quantity_returned) { %> · <%= r.quantity_returned %> already back<% } %></span>
          <% if (r.is_overdue) { %>
            <span class="st crit" style="margin-left:6px"><span class="dot"></span>overdue — <%= r.days_out %> days out</span>
          <% } %>
        </div>
        <div class="row" style="gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:flex-end">
          <div style="flex:0 0 165px"><label class="fl">Total back, out of <%= r.quantity_sent %></label>
            <input class="fi" type="number" min="0" max="<%= r.quantity_sent %>"
                   name="quantity_returned" value="<%= r.quantity_sent %>" required></div>
          <div style="flex:0 0 150px"><label class="fl">Received on</label>
            <input class="fi" type="date" name="returned_on" value="<%= todayStr %>"
                   min="<%= d10(r.dispatch_date) %>" max="<%= todayStr %>"></div>
          <div style="flex:0 0 200px"><label class="fl">Wash quality</label>
            <select class="fi" name="quality_ok">
              <option value="">— not checked —</option>
              <option value="1">Accepted</option>
              <option value="0">Rejected — rewash required</option>
            </select></div>
          <div style="flex:1 1 190px"><label class="fl">Remarks</label>
            <input class="fi" name="quality_remarks" placeholder="stains, tears, short return"></div>
          <div><button class="btn" type="submit">Receive this consignment</button></div>
        </div>
        <div class="muted" style="font-size:11.3px;margin-top:7px">
          Fewer back than went out leaves this consignment open for the balance. The shortfall is
          shown against the contract's recovery rate and multiplied by nothing.
        </div>
      </form>
    <% }); %>
  </div>
</div>
<% } %>

<%# --------------------------------------------------- 3. RETURN REGISTER
    Ordered on the RETURN, which is the only order a washing bill can be
    checked in. The window is the longest return period this running room's
    contract sets for any item — not a number chosen here. Anything not fully
    back sits at the top in red and never scrolls out of the window, because
    linen that never came back is precisely what a date window would drop. %>
<div class="card" style="margin-bottom:14px">
  <div class="card-h"><h3>Return register</h3>
    <span class="sub">returns of the last <%= windowDays %> day<%= windowDays === 1 ? '' : 's' %><%
      if (stillOut.length) { %>, and everything still out<% } %></span>
    <% if (stillOut.length) { %>
      <span class="spacer"></span>
      <span class="st crit"><span class="dot"></span><%= stillOut.length %> not back<%
        if (stillOutPieces) { %> — <%= fmtInt(stillOutPieces) %> piece<%= stillOutPieces === 1 ? '' : 's' %><% } %></span>
    <% } %></div>
  <div class="tblwrap"><table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>Back on</th><th>Item</th><th>Sent on</th><th class="num">Sent</th>
      <th class="num">Back</th><th class="num">Short</th><th class="num">Days</th>
      <th>Washing centre</th><th>Quality</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    <% retRows.forEach(function(r){ %>
      <tr<%= r.open ? ' style="background:rgba(200,40,40,.055)"' : '' %>>
        <td class="tnum">
          <% if (r.open) { %>
            <span class="st crit"><span class="dot"></span>not back</span>
            <div class="muted" style="font-size:10.5px"><%= r.days_out %> day<%= r.days_out === 1 ? '' : 's' %> out</div>
          <% } else { %><%= d10(r.returned_on) %><% } %>
        </td>
        <td><%= r.item_name %>
          <div class="muted" style="font-size:10.5px">
            <% if (r.due_days === null) { %>no period set
            <% } else { %>allowed <%= r.due_days %> day<%= r.due_days === 1 ? '' : 's' %><% } %>
          </div></td>
        <td class="tnum"><%= d10(r.dispatch_date) %></td>
        <td class="num"><%= r.quantity_sent %></td>
        <td class="num"><%= r.quantity_returned %></td>
        <td class="num"><% if (r.shortfall) { %>
              <span class="st crit"><span class="dot"></span><%= r.shortfall %></span>
            <% } else { %>—<% } %></td>
        <td class="num tnum"><% if (r.open) { %>—
          <% } else { %><%= r.days_taken %>
            <% if (r.late) { %><div class="st crit" style="font-size:10.5px"><span class="dot"></span>late</div><% } %>
          <% } %></td>
        <td><% if (r.vendor_name) { %><%= r.vendor_name %><% if (!r.is_approved) { %>
              <span class="pill r" style="margin-left:5px">not approved</span><% } %>
            <% } else { %><span class="st crit"><span class="dot"></span>not recorded</span><% } %></td>
        <td><% if (r.quality_ok === 1) { %><span class="st good"><span class="dot"></span>Accepted</span>
            <% } else if (r.quality_ok === 0) { %><span class="st crit"><span class="dot"></span>Rejected</span>
            <% } else { %><span class="st neut"><span class="dot"></span>Not checked</span><% } %>
            <% if (r.quality_remarks) { %><div class="muted" style="font-size:11.3px"><%= r.quality_remarks %></div><% } %></td>
      </tr>
    <% }); %>
    <% if (!retRows.length) { %>
      <tr><td colspan="9" class="muted">Nothing has come back in the last <%= windowDays %> days,
        and nothing is out at the wash.</td></tr>
    <% } %>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <div class="tblfoot">
    <b><%= windowDays %> days</b> is the longest return period this running room's contract sets for any
    item — at IGP the blanket cover's seven. A shorter window would drop a consignment that is still
    legitimately at the wash. <b>Days</b> is whole days between going and coming back, and <b>late</b>
    is said only where the contract sets a period; an item it is silent about is never called late.
    <b>Short</b> is what did not come back. It stays on this register however old it is — a consignment
    that never returned is the one thing a date window must not be allowed to hide.
  </div>
</div>

<div class="kpis" style="margin-bottom:14px">
  <div class="kpi"><div class="strip" style="background:var(--s1)"></div>
    <div class="lab">Dispatches on record</div><div class="val"><%= rows.length %></div>
    <div class="foot">most recent 40</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="strip" style="background:var(--warning)"></div>
    <div class="lab">Not fully returned</div><div class="val"><%= pending %></div>
    <div class="foot">sent quantity still out</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="strip" style="background:var(--critical)"></div>
    <div class="lab">Back later than the contract allows</div><div class="val"><%= overdue.length %></div>
    <div class="foot"><% if (overdue.length) { %>
      <span class="st crit"><span class="dot"></span><span data-clause="C6" data-rr="<%= rr.id %>" title="What this clause says here">clause C6</span><% if (overduePieces) { %> — <%= fmtInt(overduePieces) %> pieces<% } %></span>
      <% } else { %><span class="st good"><span class="dot"></span>all back in time</span><% } %></div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="strip" style="background:var(--critical)"></div>
    <div class="lab">Without laundry invoice</div><div class="val"><%= noInvoice %></div>
    <div class="foot"><span data-clause="C1" data-rr="<%= rr.id %>" title="What this clause says here">clause C1</span> needs the proof</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="strip" style="background:var(--critical)"></div>
    <div class="lab">Washed at a non-approved source</div>
    <div class="val"><%= unapproved.length + noVendor.length %></div>
    <div class="foot"><% if (unapproved.length || noVendor.length) { %>
      <span class="st crit"><span class="dot"></span><span data-clause="C1" data-rr="<%= rr.id %>" title="What this clause says here">clause C1</span> breach</span>
      <% } else { %><span class="st good"><span class="dot"></span>all approved</span><% } %></div></div>
</div>

<%# ------------------------------------------------- 4. DISPATCH REGISTER
    The record, ordered on the day the linen LEFT. Work is not done here. %>
<div class="card" style="margin-bottom:14px">
  <div class="card-h"><h3>Laundry dispatch register</h3><span class="sub"><%= rr.name %></span></div>
  <div class="tblwrap"><table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>Sent</th><th>Item</th><th>Washing centre</th><th class="num">Sent</th>
      <th class="num">Back</th><th>Invoice</th><th>Quality</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    <% rows.forEach(function(r){ %>
      <tr>
        <td class="tnum"><%= d10(r.dispatch_date) %>
          <% if (r.quantity_returned < r.quantity_sent) { %>
            <div class="muted" style="font-size:10.5px"><%= r.days_out %> day<%= r.days_out === 1 ? '' : 's' %> out</div>
          <% } %></td>
        <td><%= ITEMS[r.item_type] || r.item_type %>
          <div class="muted" style="font-size:10.5px">
            <% if (r.due_days === null) { %>no period set
            <% } else { %>due back in <%= r.due_days %> day<%= r.due_days === 1 ? '' : 's' %><% } %>
            <% if (r.from_pool === 'shelf') { %> · from the shelf<% } %>
          </div>
          <% if (r.is_overdue) { %>
            <div class="st crit" style="font-size:10.5px"><span class="dot"></span>overdue</div>
          <% } %></td>
        <td><% if (r.vendor_name) { %><%= r.vendor_name %><% if (!r.is_approved) { %>
              <span class="pill r" style="margin-left:5px">not approved</span><% } %>
            <% } else { %><span class="muted">not recorded</span><% } %></td>
        <td class="num"><%= r.quantity_sent %></td>
        <td class="num"><% if (r.quantity_returned < r.quantity_sent) { %>
              <span class="st warn"><span class="dot"></span><%= r.quantity_returned %></span>
            <% } else { %><%= r.quantity_returned %><% } %></td>
        <td><% if (r.invoice_no) { %><%= r.invoice_no %>
            <% } else { %><span class="st crit"><span class="dot"></span>missing</span><% } %></td>
        <td><% if (r.quality_ok === 1) { %><span class="st good"><span class="dot"></span>Accepted</span>
            <% } else if (r.quality_ok === 0) { %><span class="st crit"><span class="dot"></span>Rejected</span>
            <% } else { %><span class="st neut"><span class="dot"></span>Not checked</span><% } %>
            <% if (r.quality_remarks) { %><div class="muted" style="font-size:11.3px"><%= r.quality_remarks %></div><% } %></td>
      </tr>
    <% }); %>
    <% if (!rows.length) { %><tr><td colspan="7" class="muted">No dispatch recorded yet.</td></tr><% } %>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <div class="card-h"><h3>What the contract says</h3>
    <span class="sub">the schedule both registers run on</span></div>
  <div class="tblwrap"><table class="tbl">
    <thead><tr><th>Item</th><th class="num">Back within</th><th>Washed</th>
      <th class="num">If lost</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
    <% schedule.filter(function(x){ return x.item_type !== 'other'; }).forEach(function(x){ %>
      <tr class="li li-<%= x.item_type %>">
        <td><%= x.name %></td>
        <td class="num tnum"><% if (x.delivery_days === null) { %>—
          <% } else { %><%= x.delivery_days %> day<%= x.delivery_days === 1 ? '' : 's' %><% } %></td>
        <td class="muted" style="font-size:11.5px"><%= x.wash_frequency || '—' %><%
          if (x.per_bed) { %> · <%= x.per_bed %> per bed<% } %></td>
        <td class="num tnum"><%= x.recovery_rate === null ? '—' : 'Rs ' + Number(x.recovery_rate).toFixed(2) %></td>
      </tr>
    <% }); %>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <div class="tblfoot">
    Read off the executed contract, not off the earlier tender paper. <b>Back within</b> is what these
    registers flag on — bed sheets next day, a blanket cover in seven — and it replaced a flat 48 hours
    that was wrong in both directions at once. <b>If lost</b> is the recovery rate per unit as the contract
    prints it; <b>nothing here multiplies it</b>. A shortfall of eleven bed sheets is eleven bed sheets
    beside Rs 170 a unit, and what comes off the bill is the officer's act.
